{"at":"2026-08-09T12:37:05Z","incident":"inc-001","step":"decide_type","candidates_considered":["code_fix","config_proposal","deferred"],"code_fix_rejected_because":"RCA explicitly states the Go code is executing as designed — removing/bypassing checkProductFailure would delete the demo's deliberate fault-injection feature. Playbook 'fix the cause, don't hide the symptom' applies verbatim: the cause is not this function's existence, it is the live flag variant that a scenario owner set. A diff here would be reckless per playbook's reckless-pattern list.","config_proposal_rejected_because":"RCA already confirmed defaultVariant=off in flagd. The live variant was set on externally at runtime; rewriting the default in src/product-catalog/flags.json or src/flagd/demo.flagd.json does not override a runtime variant. Proposal would be theatre, not remediation.","toggle_rejected_because":"sre-engineer/CLAUDE.md hard rule: 'No capability may call flagd's /toggle — this project is read-only on the real target system's fault-injection state, always.' Not routed around.","chose":"deferred"}
